    "note": "Version read: Amended 2019-06-19 (Assembly's 2019-04-08 vote was on the Introduced text; later votes on this text). Sec. 26392 and 26406 (open-carry exemptions for a person turning in a found/taken gun) are listed by their lead-in only; their three paragraphs mirror 27922(a). Bill adds 'Probate Code or' to conservator lists in Penal Code 16960, 16990 and 31700(b)(9) (adds only), and Sec. 11 declares Secs. 1-2 declaratory of existing law. Sec. 27922(b) and 31700(d) add the words 'that are not subject to the applicable provisions of Sections 18000, 18005, or 34000, shall, if the person has requested the firearm and is eligible to receive it,' and strike 'shall' / 'person.' as restated."
